Subject: Iterating within file names
Message-ID: <QXl_EDh5bvA.TVb00Kldvg0J@davis-rug.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/davis-rug/c/QXl_EDh5bvA/m/TVb00Kldvg0J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

How would you go about iterating within file names so that each time my model runs it saves output with a different file name (i.e., matrix-[x].RData for my example below). Also, what would be the best format to save  two-dimensional data arrays so that they can be stacked and averaged together? Let me know if I'm not being clear enough, thanks!

for(x in 1:10){
dataset<-array(runif(50*25,1,100),c(50,25))
save(dataset,file="matrix.RData")
}

From u056871a2010712cd at groups.google.com  Mon May 13 20:37:23 2013
From: u056871a2010712cd at groups.google.com (Christopher Aden)
Date: Mon, 13 May 2013 20:37:23 +0000
Subject: Re: [D-RUG]: Iterating within file names
Message-ID: <QXl_EDh5bvA.-8TdQ_rVuTcJ@davis-rug.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <QXl_EDh5bvA.TVb00Kldvg0J@davis-rug.groups.google.com>
References: <QXl_EDh5bvA.TVb00Kldvg0J@davis-rug.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/davis-rug/c/QXl_EDh5bvA/m/-8TdQ_rVuTcJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Greg,
Try the paste function.

> test=character(10)
> for (x in 1:10) { test[x] = paste("matrix-", x, ".Rdata", sep='')}
> test
 [1] "matrix-1.Rdata"  "matrix-2.Rdata"  "matrix-3.Rdata"  "matrix-4.Rdata"
 [5] "matrix-5.Rdata"  "matrix-6.Rdata"  "matrix-7.Rdata"  "matrix-8.Rdata"
 [9] "matrix-9.Rdata"  "matrix-10.Rdata"

Then just pass save() the variable test[x] inside the for loop where you'd usually specify a file string, ie:
save(dataset, file=test[x])

HTH,
Christopher Aden

