From ub35e99045f6c74c2 at groups.google.com  Mon May 13 21:11:54 2013
From: ub35e99045f6c74c2 at groups.google.com (Vince S. Buffalo)
Date: Mon, 13 May 2013 21:11:54 +0000
Subject: Re: [D-RUG]: Iterating within file names
Message-ID: <QXl_EDh5bvA._YyLJn76JfMJ@davis-rug.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <QXl_EDh5bvA.-8TdQ_rVuTcJ@davis-rug.groups.google.com>
References: <QXl_EDh5bvA.TVb00Kldvg0J@davis-rug.groups.google.com> <QXl_EDh5bvA.-8TdQ_rVuTcJ@davis-rug.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/davis-rug/c/QXl_EDh5bvA/m/_YyLJn76JfMJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Or, more concisely:

paste0("matrix-", seq_len(10), ".Rdata")

Note that this is ok only when concatenating parts of a file name. Directories should be combined with file.path, as this is more portable. For example:

file.path("test", paste0("matrix-", seq_len(10), ".Rdata"))

Vince

