Hi Greg,

I suspect that the laply and aaply functions in the plyr package will help you out here.
library(plyr)
#make a list of file names
file.names <- as.list(paste0("matrix-", 1:NUMBER.OF.FILES, ".Rdata"))

#load each and return an array of all of them slapped together
big.array <-  laply(file.names, function(x) {
     load(x)
     return(dataset)
    })

#get a matrix of means along the first two dimensions of this array
means <- aaply(big.array, c(1,2), mean)

#get a matrix of standard deviations

SDs <- aaply(big.array, c(1,2), sd)

Also, the abind function in the abind package combines arrays and can be useful.  The

