Hi all,

This week at D-RUG we'll have a talk from Robert Hijmans. Robert is the author of the raster package - the essential way to deal with gridded spatial data in R, as well as the dismo (species distribution modeling) and geosphere (spherical trigonometry) packages. He also teaches GEO200CN - Quantitative geography, not to mention his great research on species distribution modeling <http://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=NWdPabcAAAAJ&view_op=list_works&pagesize=100> .Robert will give a talk about tools for spatial analysis in R. Come with your spatial/geographic analysis questions!

Note that this week's D-RUG will be in 2120J Wickson - this is the room just to the right of our regular meeting space. It will at the usual time: 1-3 PM, with the usual snacks.

See you there!

Noam

